1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:06,670
This video shows you how to handle values that are missing from a record.

2
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:09,344
Here's the Code step from the last video.

3
00:00:09,344 --> 00:00:13,030
It reads each log line into the field app, with types.

4
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:15,414
Not every line has every field.

5
00:00:15,414 --> 00:00:21,790
This one is background work, with no request, so it has no status and no duration.

6
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:25,070
A field a record lacks reads as null.

7
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:30,457
Now mark each request as a success or a failure, with a ternary: a condition,

8
00:00:30,457 --> 00:00:36,190
a value for true after the question mark, and a value for false after the colon.

9
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:40,790
But this record made no request, and it says success.

10
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:45,679
A comparison such as greater than is false when one side is null.

11
00:00:45,679 --> 00:00:49,310
So the ternary took the value after the colon.

12
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:53,190
Set outcome only where there is a status.

13
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:58,075
Now this record has no outcome, and the requests keep theirs.

14
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:04,681
Every record needs a message.

15
00:01:04,681 --> 00:01:10,030
Take app.msg, or the whole line for a record that has no msg.

16
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:13,390
Two question marks give a fallback for null.

17
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:18,569
The stack trace has no app, so its message is the line itself.

18
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:22,828
Its text is now in message and in app's fields.

19
00:01:22,828 --> 00:01:26,248
Writing null to a field removes it.

20
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,353
Save.

21
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:33,101
Check on learning.

22
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:36,513
A record has no status.

23
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:40,564
What does app.status >= 400 ?

24
00:01:40,564 --> 00:01:44,935
"failure" : "success" give?

25
00:01:49,335 --> 00:01:49,913
success.

26
00:01:49,913 --> 00:01:53,236
The comparison is false when one side is null,

27
00:01:53,236 --> 00:01:57,232
so the ternary takes the value after the colon.

28
00:01:58,132 --> 00:02:02,030
How do you give a fallback for a value that is null?

29
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:12,162
With two question marks, as in app.msg ??

30
00:02:12,162 --> 00:02:13,321
log.

31
00:02:14,221 --> 00:02:17,979
Next, you catch bad data with try.
